  <main id="main-content" class="seo-page"><div class="seo-answer"><strong>Direct answer:</strong> Depression and anxiety at Mind Grace Neuropsychiatric Clinic are treated with evidence-based psychiatric care and psychotherapy, usually combining medication where needed with counselling such as CBT for lasting relief.</div>
<section class="seo-hero"><p class="seo-kicker">Common mental-health concerns</p><h1>Support for depression, anxiety, and panic</h1><p class="seo-lead">Persistent worry, low mood, panic, irritability, poor sleep, or loss of interest can affect everyday life. A consultation can help clarify what is happening and what support may fit.</p><div class="seo-actions"><a class="btn" href="/book">Request a consultation</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/psychiatry">Psychiatry pathway</a></div></section><section class="seo-section"><h2>What may be explored</h2><div class="seo-grid"><article class="seo-card"><h3>Your pattern</h3><p>Onset, duration, triggers, physical symptoms, sleep, functioning, and previous support may be discussed.</p></article><article class="seo-card"><h3>Treatment options</h3><p>Depending on the assessment, options may include therapy, practical strategies, medication discussion, or referral.</p></article><article class="seo-card"><h3>Ongoing support</h3><p>Follow-up and adjustment are guided by response, preferences, safety, and clinical judgement.</p></article></div><div class="seo-note"><strong>Not a diagnosis:</strong> Similar symptoms can have different causes. A clinician must assess you before recommending treatment.</div></section><section class="seo-section"><p>Related: <a href="/ocd-panic-ptsd">OCD, panic, and PTSD</a> · <a href="/process">What to expect</a> · <a href="/emergency">Emergency help</a></p></section>    
  </main>
